{
 "note": "fl_sound_shape: words -> moves. 'inst': nudges of the channel's own instrument controls, found by their FL parameter names (roles below), as a share of the knob's range at amount 'medium'. 'fx': stock effects on the channel's mixer track (controls in real units through the plugin maps; numbers listed in 'scale' grow with the amount), 'eq': Parametric EQ 2 moves. 'alt': used when the user's FL edition doesn't own 'plugin'. 'intents': what the before/after measurement checks. 'fx_tune': settings for effects OTHER words add (never adds the effect itself; a lower Hz wins), e.g. a darker reverb/delay tail. A word with the 'darker' intent wins on the top end: boosts at 2 kHz and up from other words are left out, the EQ goes after the reverb/delay so their tails are darkened too. A user copy in the state folder's sound/ wins.",
